$DATUM 2-(2-Bromopbenylsulfanyl)-benzonitrile (1b). 2-Bromothiophenol (1.20 mL,
10.0 mmol), 2-fluorobenzonitrile (1.20 mL, 11.0 mmol) and freshly ground
K2CO3 (2.1 g, 15 mmol) were stirred in DMF (9 mL) at 100°C under N2 for
24 hours. At rt sat. NH4Cl (25 mL) was added. Extraction with Et2O (5×25
mL) and the combined organic phases were washed with brine (25 mL).
Drying (Na2SO4) and evaporation of the solvent gave the crude product
which was purified by FC (heptane/EtOAc) yielding 2.95 g (99 %) of 1b as
colorless crystals. mp 92-93 °C (heptane/EtOAc), Rf (heptane/EtOAc 4:1)
0.47. 1H-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): 7.18-7.24 (m, 2H), 7.27-7.30 (m, 2H), 7.36
(td, 1H, J=7.6,1.2 Hz), 7.49 (td, 1H, J=7.6, 1.6 Hz), 7.64-7.73 (m, 2H).
13C-NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): 114.3 (s), 116.7 (s), 126.9 (s), 127.4 (d),
128.3 (d), 129.7 (d), 131.5 (d), 133.2 (d), 133.6 (d), 133.7 (d), 134.0
(d), 134.2 (s); 139.6 (s). Anal. Calcd. for C13H8BrNS: C, 53.81; H, 2.78;
N, 4.83. Found: C, 54.06; H, 2.82, N, 4.64.
