$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Ethyl 5-nitrobenzo[b]thiophene-2-carboxylate (1) t-BuOK (14 g, 125 mmol)
was dissolved in cooled absolute EtOH (150 mL) and ethyl mercaptoacetate
(15.6 g, 130 mmol) was added to the formed solution in one portion. After
15 min of stirring at rt, 2-chloro-5-nitrobenzaldehyde (20 g, 108 mmol)
was added in portions, keeping the temperature below 50°C. The formed
suspension was stirred at rt for 1 h and refluxed for 30 min. Fifty mL of
water was added at this point, and the reaction mixture was allowed to
cool to 4°C. Filtration of the residue followed by washings with water
and cold EtOH. 26.8 g (99%) of light-yellow powder. mp 165-166°C
(lit.[15] 165°C); 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.45 (t, 3H, J=7.1 Hz), 4.46
(q, 2H, J=7.1 Hz), 8.00 (d, 1H, J=9.0 Hz), 8.19 (s, 1H), 8.31 (dd, 1H,
J=9.0 Hz, J=1.8 Hz), 8.78 (d, 1H, J=1.8 Hz); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ
14.3, 62.2, 120.8, 121.1, 123.6, 130.4, 137.8, 138.4, 145.9, 147.3, 161.8
(lit.[15] 1H NMR).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Convenient and efficient synthesis of 2-methyl-5-nitrobenzo[b]thiophene
and its derivatives
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Migulin, Vasily A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2016), 46(4), 332-337

