$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the palladium-catalyzed coupling of aryl chlorides
with aromatic thiols: The appropriate quantity of stock solution B was
added to a 4 mL vial containing the aryl chloride (1.00 mmol) and
potasium tert-butoxide (123 mg, 1.10 mmol) in 1.5 mL of toluene. The
aromatic thiol (1.00 mmol) was then added, and the vial sealed with a cap
containing a PTFE septum. The mixture was heated at 110 ºC until the
chloroarene was consumed, as determined by GC. Silica gel (0.5 g) was
then added, and solvents were evaporated under reduced pressure. The
crude residue was purified by column chromatography on silica gel using
hexane or a mixture of hexane and ethyl acetate as eluent. Aryl sulfides
were isolated in the yields reported in Table 1. 4-Methoxyphenyl phenyl
sulfide (Table 1, entry 2).2 100 μL of stock solution B were used. 98%
yield. Colorless liquid. Colorless liquid. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 7.23 (d, J =
8.8 Hz, 2H), 7.06-7.02 (m, 2H),7.00-6.93 (m, 3H), 6.71 (d, J = 8.8 Hz,
2H), 3.62 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 159.7, 138.5, 135.3 (2C), 128.8
(2C), 128.1 (2C), 125.7, 124.2, 114.9 (2C), 55.3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A General and Long-Lived Catalyst for the Palladium-Catalyzed Coupling of
Aryl Halides with Thiols
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Fernandez-Rodriguez, Manuel A.; Shen, Qilong; Hartwig, John F.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2006), 128(7), 2180-2181

