$DATUM 4-Methoxyphenyl Phenyl Sulfide (3a); Typical Procedure Cs2CO3 (325.8 mg,
1.0 mmol), CuBr (14.3 mg, 0.10 mmol), and L3 (26.6 mg, 0.10 mmol) were
added to a 10-mL reaction tube equipped with a septum. The tube was
evacuated and back-filled with N2 and MeCN (2.0 mL) was added to the
mixture at r.t. To the resulting soln 4-iodoanisole (117 mg, 0.50 mmol)
was added followed by PhSH (60.6 mg, 0.55 mmol), and the mixture was
heated at 82 °C for 10 h. After complete disappearance of 4-iodoanisole
(TLC monitoring), the mixture was allowed to cool to r.t. The crude
residue was directly purified by column chromatography (silica gel,
EtOAc-hexanes). The product as a colorless oil. Rf = 0.29; IR (neat):
3003, 2927, 2836, 825, 737, 689, 639 cm-1. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
3.65 (s, 3 H), 6.76 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2 H), 6.99-7.11 (m, 5 H), 7.29 (d, J
= 8.4 Hz, 2 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 55.46, 115.11, 124.45,
125.88, 128.35, 129.04, 135.45, 138.71, 159.95. HRMS: m/z [M + H]+ calcd
for C13H13OS: 217.0687; found: 217.0681.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study (optimized on catalysts and solvents), Ullmann
reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An efficient, mild and intermolecular Ullmann-type synthesis of
thioethers catalyzed by a diol-copper(I) complex
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Prasad, D. J. C.; Sekar, Govindasamy
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2010), (1), 79-84

