$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure (Table 1, entry 10): Cs2CO3
(661 mg, 2.03 mmol), CuI (19 mg, 0.1 mmol, 10 mol%), and
1,1,1-tris(hydroxymethyl)ethane (12 mg, 0.1 mmol, 10 mol%) were added to
a screw-capped test tube with a septum. The tube was evacuated with
heating and back-filled with nitrogen three times. Dioxane (1.8 mL), DMF
(0.2 mL), iodobenzene (0.112 mL, 1.0 mmol), and 2-pyrrolidone (0.094 mL,
1.2 mmol) were added by syringe at room temperature. After the septum of
tube was exchanged with a Teflon screw-cap, the reaction mixture was
heated at 110 °C for 24 h, and then allowed to cool to room temperature.
The reaction mixture was directly passed through celite. After rinsed
with further 50 mL of ethyl acetate, the combined filtrate was evaporated
by vacuum to yield the crude product. The residue was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel using hexane/ethyl acetate (1:1) as eluent
to give a white solid of 1-phenylpyrrolidin-2-one (158.1 mg, 98 %).
1-Phenylpyrrolidin-2-one(Table 2, entry 1)
1-Methoxy-4-(phenylthio)benzene(Table 3, entry 2 and 5) Colorless oil; 1H
NMR(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.40(2H, d, J=8.4 Hz), 7.09-7.23(5H, m), 6.88(2H,
d, J=8.4 Hz), 3.78(3H, s). 13C NMR(100 MHz, CDCl3 ) δ 55.2, 114.9, 124.2,
125.7, 128.1, 128.8, 135.2, 138.5, 159.7.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 1,1,1-Tris(hydroxymethyl)ethane as a New, Efficient, and Versatile Tripod
Ligand for Copper-Catalyzed Cross-Coupling Reactions of Aryl Iodides with
Amides, Thiols, and Phenols
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Chen, Yao-Jung; Chen, Hsin-Hung
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2006), 8(24), 5609-5612

