$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A General procedure for the one-pot C-S cross-coupling reaction. To a
glass vial charged with PEG-600 (3 mL) was added nitroaryl halide (0.5
mmol), thiol (0.75 mmol), and KOH (84 mg, 3 equiv). The resulting mixture
was stirred at 100 °C and monitored by TLC. Upon completion of the
reaction (approx. 2 h), the mixture was cooled to room temperature,
poured into water (10 mL), and extracted several times with ethyl acetate
(15×3 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with water, dried over
Na2SO4, and filtered. The solvent was removed in vacuo and the residue
was purified by column chromatography (silica gel, eluent: hexane/ethyl
acetate) to afford the aryl sulfide product. 4-(octylthio)benzenamine
(3a). Obtained as a yellow oil in 92% yield. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.26-7.22(td, 2 H), 6.62-6.60 (d, 2 H), 3.58 (br s, 2 H), 2.78-2.75(t,
2H), 1.59-1.53 (quint, 2 H), 1.40-1.37(m, 2H), 1.26(m, 8H), 0.90-0.87(t,
3H) ppm; 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 145.6, 133.5, 123.7, 115.5, 36.3,
31.7, 29.3, 29.1, 29.0, 28.6, 22.5, 14.0 ppm; HR EIMS 237.1557 m/z
(calcd. for C14H23NS: 237.1551).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM One-Pot Synthesis of Amine-Substituted Aryl Sulfides and
Benzo[b]thiophene Derivatives
