$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Experimental Section. Typical Procedure for
Benzothiazole-2(3H)-thione Formation as Illustrated by the Preparation of
6-Fluoro-1,3-benzothiazole-2(3H)-thione (3a). 2,4-Difluoroaniline (15.0
g, 116.2 mmol, 1.0 equiv) and potassium O-ethyl xanthate (41.0 g, 255.6
mmol, 2.2 equiv) were heated in anhydrous DMF (75 mL) at 95 °C (internal
temperature) for 4 h under nitrogen. The reaction mixture was then cooled
to room temperature, diluted with water (150 mL), and acidified to pH 3-4
by adding 1 N HCl solution (200 mL). The suspension formed on
acidification was stirred for 30 min and filtered under vacuum.
[2-(Ethylthio)-4-fluorophenyl]amine (7): 98% yield. 1H NMR (DMSO-d6) δ
7.01 (dd, J= 9.3, J= 2.9, 1H), 6.84 (dt, J= 8.4, J= 2.8, 1H), 6.67 (dd,
J= 8.8, J= 5.3, 1H), 5.05 (s, 2H), 2.79 (q, J= 7.2, 2H), 1.14 (t, J= 7.2,
3H); 13C NMR (DMSO-d6) δ 154.1 (d, JC-F= 231.0), 145.6, 119.1 (d, J=
21.4), 118.0 (d, J= 8.0), 115.6 (d, J= 29.5), 115.5 (d, J= 15.5), 28.2,
15.7; 19F NMR (DMSO-d6) δ -128.9. ESI-MS m/z (MH +) 172. Anal. Calcd. for
C8H10FNS: C, 56.11; H, 5.89; N, 8.18. Found: C, 56.06; H, 5.83, N, 8.07.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
