$DATUM 4,5-Bis(4-tert-butylphenylthio)phthalonitrile (2f)
4,5-dichlorophthalonitrile (100 mg, 0.5 mmol) and K2CO3 (280 mg, 2.0
mmol) were added to a solution of 4-tert-butylbenzenethiol (0.4 mL, 2
mmol) in DMSO. After stirred for 20 h at room temperature, the reaction
was quenched with water. The mixture was extracted with CHCl3 and washed
with 5 % Na2CO3 solution and water. The organic layer was dried over
MgSO4, and concentrated in vacuo. The product was purified by silica gel
column chromatography (CHCl3-nhexane 5:1). Title compound was obtained
(224 mg, 98%) as white powder. 500 MHz 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ = 7.54 (d, 4H, J
= 8.0 Hz), 7.48 (d, 4H, J = 8.0 Hz), 6.98 (s, 2H), 1.39 (s, 18H). 125 MHz
13C-NMR (CDCl3) δ (ppm): 154.3, 144.3, 135.1, 129.4, 127.8, 124.6, 115.6,
111.3, 35.0, 31.2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Design, Synthesis, and Properties of Phthalocyanine Complexes with
Main-Group Elements Showing Main Absorption and Fluorescence beyond 1000
nm
