$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: EXPERIMENTAL A 25-mL reaction tube was charged
with 2-haloaniline 1 (0.6 mmol), potassium O-ethyl dithiocarbonate 2 (1.8
mmol), FeF3(0.06 mmol), 2,2′-bis (diphenylphosphino)-1,1′-binaphthyl
(0.03 mmol), and DMF (4 mL). The reaction vessel was flushed with argon
three times and sealed. Then the mixture was stirred electromagnetically
in an oil bath at 110°C for 3-21 h. The reaction process was monitored by
thin-layer chromatography (TLC) on silica gel. After the reaction was
completed, the reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature, and then
4 mL HCl (3mol/L) was added and stirred for another 30 min. Then the
reaction mixture solution was extracted by ethyl acetate (3× 20 mL).
Subsequently, the combined organic solution was dried by anhydrous sodium
sulfate and the target product was purified by silica-gel column
chromatography (eluent: petroleum ether/ethyl acetate). The corresponding
pure products 3a-3h. 2-mercaptobenzothiazole (3a)1
6-carbonitrile-2-mercaptobenzothiazole (3g) 1 3g was obtained as a light
yellow solid. M.p. 273-275°C; 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO, TMS): δ 14.12 (brs,
1H), 8.23 (d, 1H, J = 1.5 Hz), 7.82 (dd, 1H, J1 = 8.5 Hz, J2 = 2.0 Hz),
7.40 (d, 1H, J = 8.5 Hz); 13C NMR (125 MHz, DMSO, TMS): δ 191.4, 144.2,
130.9, 129.9, 125.7, 118.3, 112.7, 106.0; MS (EI+): m/z calcd for
C8H5N2S2 [M+H]+: 192.99, found 192.2; Anal. Calcd. for C8H4N2S2: C,
49.98; H, 2.10; N, 14.57; Found: C, 50.21; H, 1.89; N, 14.51.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed vessel used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient, Iron-Catalyzed Synthesis of 2-Mercaptobenzothiazole Through
S-Arylation/Heterocyclization of 2-Haloaniline with Potassium Xanthate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Gao, Min; Lou, Chunqing; Zhu, Ning; Qin, Weijing; Suo, Quanling; Han,
Limin; Hong, Hailong
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2015), 45(20), 2378-2385

