$DATUM ethyl 5-amino-6-nitrobenzo[b]thiophene-2-carboxylate (4). A 20 mL
microwave tube was charged with 3 (700 mg, 2.9 mmol), ethyl
2-mercaptoacetate (421 mg, 3.5 mmol), K2CO3 (590 mg, 4.3 mmol), CuO
nanopowder (100 mg, 1.3 mmol), DMSO (10 mL) and sealed with a Teflon cap.
Using a Biotage microwave reactor with stirring, the reaction mixture was
heated to 80°C for 2 h under the power of 10 W and a presure of 1 atm.
After cooling, the mixture was poured into water. The aqueous phase was
extracted with ethyl acetate (3 × 25 mL) and the organic layer was dried
over Na2SO4. The solvent was removed under vacuum. The product was
obtained without further purification. red powder, yield: (756 mg,
97.9%). 1H-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3, δ):8.67(s, 1H), 7.81(s, 1H), 7.25(s, 1H),
5.84 (s, 2H), 4.42(m, 2H), 1.42(t, J= 6.9 Hz, 3H). 13C-NMR (75 MHz, DMSO,
δ):162.18, 145.35, 143.64, 140.71, 133.54, 129.57, 128.64, 121.86,
113.48, 62.50,14.75. EI-MS: Calcd. for [C11H10N2O4S]+ : 266.04; Found:
265.9.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, 10 W used, sealed tube used
