$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (III) General procedure for
palladium-catalyzed arylation of sulfenate anions under biphasic
conditions To a solution of tris(dibenzylideneacetone)dipalladium (5
mol%) in toluene (500 μL) was added xantphos (10 mol%). The solution was
stirred at room temperature for 5 min. Then, a solution of iodide
substrate (0.6 mmol in 1.5 mL of toluene), β-sulfinylester (0.5 mmol in
1.5 mL of toluene), 3.5 mL of distilled water and 50% aqueous KOH
solution (10 mmol) were successively added. The resulting biphasic system
was stirred vigorously at 70 °C for 2 h. Then, after cooling to room
temperature, the aqueous phase was extracted twice with dichloromethane,
the collected organic layers were dried over anhydrous MgSO4 and the
solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The crude product was
purified by flash chromatography. bis(p-tolyl) sulfoxide 3a:
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Aryl sulfoxides via palladium-catalyzed arylation of sulfenate anions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
