$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the palladium-catalyzed coupling of aryl chlorides
with aliphatic thiols: The appropriate quantity of stock solution A was
added to a 4 mL vial containing the aryl chloride (1.00 mmol) and sodium
tert-butoxide (106 mg, 1.10 mmol) in 1.5 mL of DME. The aliphatic thiol
(1.00 mmol) was then added, and the vial sealed with a cap containing a
PTFE septum. The mixture was heated at 110 ºC until the chloroarene was
consumed, as determined by GC. Silica gel (0.5 g) was added, and the
solvents were evaporated under reduced pressure. The crude residue was
purified by column chromatography on silica gel using hexane or a mixture
of hexane and ethyl acetate as eluent. Aryl sulfides were isolated in the
yields reported in Table 1. 4-Methoxyphenyl octyl sulfide (Table 1, entry
1). 1 100 μL of stock solution A were used. 98% yield. Colorless liquid.
Colorless liquid. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 7.25 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H), 6.76 (d, J
= 8.6 Hz, 2H), 3.71 (s, 3H), 2.73 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H), 1.50 (quint, J =
7.4 Hz, 2H), 1.30 (quint, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H), 1.22-1.14 (m, 8H), 0.80 (t, J
= 7.1 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 158.6, 132.8 (2C), 126.9, 114.4 (2C),
55.2, 35.7, 31.7, 29.3, 29.09, 29.06, 28.6, 22.6, 14.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A General and Long-Lived Catalyst for the Palladium-Catalyzed Coupling of
Aryl Halides with Thiols
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Fernandez-Rodriguez, Manuel A.; Shen, Qilong; Hartwig, John F.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2006), 128(7), 2180-2181

