$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4-Fluorophenyl 2-Naphthyl Sulfide (3c). To a
suspension of Pd(OAc)2 (4.5 mg, 0.020 mmol, 4.0 mol %) and Xantphos (12.1
mg, 0.021 mmol, 4.2 mol %) in DMF (1.0 mL) was added 2-bromonaphthalene
(103.5 mg, 0.50 mmol) in DMF (0.5 mL) at room temperature under a
nitrogen atmosphere. After being stirred for 5 min, (4-F-C6H4S)3In (83.0
mg, 0.167 mmol) and DIPEA (87.0 μL, 0.50 mmol) in DMF (1.0 mL) was
transferred via double-ended needle and the mixture was stirred at 100 °C
for 4 h. The reaction mixture was quenched with sat. NaHCO3 solution (1.0
mL). The aqueous layer was extracted with ether (3 × 20 mL), and the
combined organics were washed with water (10 mL) and sat. NaCl solution
(10 mL), dried with anhydrous MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The residue was purified by silica gel column
chromatography (hexane) to give 3c as a white crystal (116.0 mg, 91%).
4-Methoxyphenyl phenyl sulfide (3n) 3 : Colorless oil.
