$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the palladium-catalyzed
coupling of functionalized aryl chlorides with aliphatic and aromatic
thiols. The appropriate quantity of stock solution A was added to a 4 mL
vial containing the aryl chloride (1.00 mmol) and NaOtBu (230 mg, 2.40
mmol) in 1.5 mL of DME. The thiol (1.00 mmol) was then added, and the
vial sealed with a cap containing a PTFE septum. The mixture was heated
at 110 ºC until the chloroarene was consumed, as determined by GC. Silica
gel (0.5 g) was added, and the solvents were evaporated under reduced
pressure. The crude residue was purified by column chromatography on
silica gel using hexane or mixtures of hexane and ethyl acetate as
eluent. Aryl sulfides were isolated in the yields reported in Table 1.
2-Octylsulfanylphenol (Table 1, entry 29). 13 A solution of Pd(OAc)2 (4.4
mg) and CyPF-t- Bu (11 mg) in DME (1 mL) was used as catalyst. 97% yield.
Yellow liquid. Yellow liquid. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 7.38 (dd, J = 7.6 Hz and
1.5 Hz, 1H), 7.17 (dt, J = 7.6 Hz and 1.5 Hz, 1H), 6.90 (d, J = 8.1 Hz,
1H), 6.80-6.76 (m, 1H), 6.70 (bs, 1 H), 2.60 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H),
1.50-1.43 (m, 2H), 1.31-1.17 (m, 10H), 0.79 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR
(CDCl3): δ 156.8, 135.8, 130.8, 120.6, 119.1, 114.6, 36.7, 31.7, 29.5,
29.04, 28.98, 28.5, 22.5, 14.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A General and Long-Lived Catalyst for the Palladium-Catalyzed Coupling of
Aryl Halides with Thiols
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
