$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Ethyl 4-Methyl-2-(4-(methylthio)-3-nitrophenyl)thiazole-5-carboxylate
(9{2,1}). To a solution of compound 8{2} (0.5 g, 1.5 mmol) in THF (5 mL)
was added sodium methane thiolate (0.13 g, 1.8 mmol). The reaction
mixture stirred for 1 h at room temperature. The resulting precipitate
was filtered and washed with THF and ethyl acetate to afford a yellow
solid product. Ethyl
4-Methyl-2-(4-(methylthio)-3-nitrophenyl)thiazole-5-carboxylate (9{2,1}),
yellow solid, (0.5 g, 97%) 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.83 (d, J = 2.0 Hz,
1H), 8.16 (dd, J = 8.5, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 7.45 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 1H), 4.37 (q, J
= 7.1 Hz, 2H), 2.79 (s, 3H), 2.56 (s, 3H), 1.40 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H); 13C
NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 166.45, 161.97, 161.33, 145.54, 142.27, 130.91,
129.48, 126.22, 124.11, 122.61, 61.51, 17.53, 16.16, 14.36.
