$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM [3-(Phenylthio)benzyl]amine (15). A microwave vial containing CuI (41 mg,
0.22 mmol) and K2CO3 (1.20 g, 8.6 mmol) was evacuated and backfilled with
argon (3 cycles). 2-Propanol (5 mL), ethylene glycol (0.48 mL, 8.6 mmol),
3-iodobenzylamine (0.57 mL, 4.3 mmol) and thiophenol (0.44 mL, 4.3 mmol)
were added at room temperature. The reaction mixture was heated in the
microwave at 140 °C for 20 minutes. Then, the solvent was evaporated
under reduced pressure and the residue was purified by chromatography
(DCM/EtOAc, 9:1). The resulting oil was dried under reduced pressure at
70 °C to remove ethylene glycol, yielding the title pure compound. Brown
syrup, 97% yield. Rf (DCM/EtOAc, 1:1) 0.71; IR (ATR) ν 3428, 1579, 1473;
1H NMR (methanol-d4) δ 3.98 (s, 2H, CH2), 7.26-7.41 (m, 9H, 9CHAr); 13C
NMR (methanol-d4) δ 44.7 (CH2), 128.2, 128.7 (2CH), 128.8 (C), 130.5
(2CH), 130.9, 131.5, 131.6 (3CH), 132.7 (2CH), 138.5 (2C); ESI-MS 216.1
(M + H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, thermal, solvothermal
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthetic Inhibitors of Bacterial Cell Division Targeting the GTP-Binding
Site of FtsZ
