$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the coupling of p-halotoluenes with 1-octanethiol
and thiophenol; compared rates and catalytic activity of the different
haloarenes: The appropriate quantity of stock solution A or B was added
to a 4 mL vial containing the aryl halide (1.00 mmol) and NaOtBu (106 mg,
1.10 mmol) in 1.5 mL of DME. The thiol (1.00 mmol) was then added, and
the vial sealed with a cap containing a PTFE septum. The mixture was
heated at 110 °C until the haloarene was consumed, as determined by GC
(reaction times reported in Scheme 2). Silica gel (0.5 g) was added, and
the solvents were evaporated under reduced pressure. The crude residue
was purified by column chromatography on silica gel using hexane as
eluent. The corresponding sulfide was isolated in the yields reported in
Scheme 2 and Table 1. 4-Methylphenyl octyl sulfide, yield 97% 1H NMR
(CDCl3): δ 7.10 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H), 6.95 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H), 2.73 (t, J
= 7.4 Hz, 2H), 2.17 (s, 3H), 1.48 (quint, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H), 1.26 (quint, J
= 7.4 Hz, 2H), 1.17-1.08 (m, 8H), 0.74 (t, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR
(CDCl3): δ 135.7, 133.1, 129.7 (2C), 129.5 (2C), 34.3, 31.7, 29.2, 29.10,
29.06, 28.7, 22.6, 20.9, 14.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM yield depends on reaction conditions (temp. and time)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A General, Efficient, and Functional-Group-Tolerant Catalyst System for
the Palladium-Catalyzed Thioetherification of Aryl Bromides and Iodides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Fernandez-Rodriguez, Manuel A.; Hartwig, John F.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2009), 74(4), 1663-1672

