$DATUM phenyl-3-methoxyphenylsulfide 3-Bromoanisole (3.39 mL, 26.73 mmol, 1.0
equiv), 2-propanol (30 mL), potassium hydroxide (3.47 g, 53.46 mmol, 2.0
equiv), tetrakis (triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (154 mg, 0.134 mmol,
0.005 equiv), (S)-BINAP (166 mg., 0.267 mmol, 0.01 equiv) and
benzenethiol (2.74 mL, 26.73 mmol, 1.0 equiv) were heated under a
nitrogen atmosphere for 20-22 h at 83 °C. After the reaction was
completed it was cooled (<30 °C) and quenched with water (30 mL) which
resulted in a small exotherm (~6 °C) and formation of an oil. The
resultant mixture was allowed to granulate for 1 h at 10-15 °C. Extracted
with dichloromethane, brine and dried over magnesium sulfate, , filtered,
concentrated to dryness. Obtained a red oil3, 5.6 g.
phenyl-3-methoxyphenylsulfide, Yield 97% m/z 216; C13H12OS requires: C,
72.2; H, 5.59; S, 14.8. Found: C, 72.0; H, 5.43; S, 14.8%; 1H NMR (400
MHz, d6-DMSO) δ 7.33 (m, 6H), 6.89 (m, 3H), 3.75 (s, 3H); IR (cm-1) νmax;
1590, 1477, 1247, 1230.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Migita reaction
